\label{rem:repmodels}
Viewed as a full subcategory of $\mathrm{Fun}(BG,\cat D(R)) \simeq \cat D(R[G)])$

equipped with the pointwise symmetric monoidal structure, the category $\mathrm{rep}(G,R)$ can be identified as the bounded derived category of objects whose underlying complex of $R$-modules is perfect. If $R$ is regular, this in turn is equivalent to the full subcategory of complexes all of whose modules are finitely generated projective $R$-modules. This is also equivalent to the category of perfect complexes on the stack $[\mathrm{Spec}(R)/G]$ as considered by Lau, see \cite[Prop.~3.1]{lau_spcdmstacks} and the discussion around it.

By \cite[Cor.~6.21]{MathewNaumannNoel17}, there is a fully faithful symmetric monoidal exact functor
