        \cat D(K) \ar[r] & \cat D(K\otimes\prod_{\frak p}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}).}
    }
\end{equation}
Let $\mathrm{Cat}_{\infty}$ be the $\infty$-category of $\infty$-categories. The Cartesian product equips $\mathrm{Cat}_{\infty}$ with the structure of a symmetric monoidal $\infty$-category (\cite[\S2.4.1]{HALurie}) and we denote the corresponding $\infty$-category of symmetric monoidal $\infty$-categories by $\mathrm{CAlg}(\mathrm{Cat}_{\infty})$. Viewing $BG$ as an $\infty$-groupoid and using the point-wise monoidal structure, the functor $\mathrm{Fun}(BG,-)\colon \mathrm{Cat}_{\infty} \to \mathrm{Cat}_{\infty}$ extends to a limit preserving functor
\[
\xymatrix{\mathrm{Fun}(BG,-)\colon \mathrm{CAlg}(\mathrm{Cat}_{\infty}) \ar[r] & \mathrm{CAlg}(\mathrm{Cat}_{\infty}).}
\]
The image of \eqref{eq:derfracturesquare} under this functor gives a pullback square of symmetric monoidal $\infty$-categories
