\label{cor:arithmeticstmodltg1}
The completion maps $\cat O \to \cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}$ induce a symmetric monoidal equivalence
\begin{equation}\label{eq:stmodfracture1}
    \vcenter{
        \xymatrix{\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O) \ar[r]^-{\sim} & \prod_{\frak p\mid |G|}\mathrm{StMod}(G, \cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}).}
    }
\end{equation}
Here, the product is indexed on all prime ideals of $\cat O$ that divide the order of $G$.

\begin{equation}\label{eq:stmodfracture1}
    \vcenter{
        \xymatrix{\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O) \ar[r]^-{\sim} & \prod_{\frak p\mid |G|}\mathrm{StMod}(G, \cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}).}
    }
\end{equation}

Applying the finite localization functor $\rho^*$ from \eqref{eq:stmodquot} to the decategorification of the pullback square \eqref{eq:repfracture} yields a pullback square in $\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O)$:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:stmodfracturesquare}
    \vcenter{
        \xymatrix{\mathbb{1} \simeq \rho^*(\cat O) \ar[r] \ar[d] & \rho^*(\prod_{\frak p}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}) \ar[d] \\
        \rho^*(K) \ar[r] & \rho^*(K\otimes\prod_{\frak p}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}).}
    }
\end{equation}
As in the proof of \cref{cor:stmodcharacteristic}, both domain and codomain of the bottom horizontal functor are trivial, hence it is an equivalence. It follows that the top horizontal functor in \eqref{eq:stmodfracturesquare} is an equivalence $\mathbb{1} \simeq \rho^*(\prod_{\frak p}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p})$ of commutative ring objects. Separating the part where the order of $G$ is invertible thus gives an equivalence 
\[
\mathbb{1} \simeq \rho^*\prod_{\frak p\mid |G|}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p} \times \rho^*\prod_{\frak p\nmid |G|}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}.
\]
The order of $G$ is invertible in $\prod_{\frak p\nmid |G|}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}$, so by another application of \cref{cor:stmodcharacteristic}, the second factor vanishes. Since the set of prime ideals in $\cat O$ dividing $|G|$ is finite, we get symmetric monoidal equivalences
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O) & \simeq \mathrm{Mod}_{\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O)}(\mathbb{1}) \\
& \simeq \mathrm{Mod}_{\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O)}(\rho^*\textstyle{\prod_{\frak p\nmid |G|}\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p}}) \\
& \simeq \textstyle{\prod_{\frak p\nmid |G|}\mathrm{Mod}_{\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cat O)}(\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p})} \\
& \simeq \textstyle{\prod_{\frak p\nmid |G|}\mathrm{StMod}(G,\cdvr{\cat O}{\frak p})},
\end{align*}
where the last equivalence follows from \cref{rem:etalecoeffbasechange}.

\begin{equation}\label{eq:stmodfracturesquare}
