\label{def:exlocalizing}
Let $\cat E$ be an exact category. A \emph{thick} subcategory $\cat S \subseteq \cat E$ is a full subcategory which satisfies the following closure properties:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $\cat S$ is closed under direct summands. 
        \item If $0\to X \to Y \to Z \to 0$ is an exact sequence in $\cat E$ such that two terms of it are in $\cat S$, then so is the third.  
    \end{itemize}
For an exact category $\cat E$ which admits set-indexed coproducts, a thick subcategory of $\cat E$ is called a \emph{localizing} subcategory if it is also closed under set-indexed coproducts. If $\cat E$ is additionally equipped with an exact symmetric monoidal structure $\otimes$, we say that $\cat S$ is a thick tensor ideal or localizing tensor ideal if it is a thick subcategory or localizing subcategory which is additionally closed under $\otimes$, respectively.

